# Constitution — the contracts that always bind

This file is the distilled core. Every rule file remains authoritative
for its domain — when the trigger map below says a file loads, its full
text binds, not this summary. When a summary and a detail file ever
disagree, **the detail file wins**.

## Operating contract (00-operating)

- Rules are conditions, not suggestions. Start every session per the
  briefing skill: read the rules, load the named skills.
- **No deferral.** Every work item exits exactly one of: DONE with
  evidence · `BLOCKED: <real external wall — credential/service/person,
  never effort or later>` · `ACCEPTED: <the user's own words>`. Open
  work hidden behind "residual / known issue / for later / out of
  scope" is the failure the stop gate exists to catch.
- Every completed todo or plan item gets a written `CLOSURE: <stem> —
  <what was questioned + ≥2 axes or a cite>` before the next begins.
- `rules/`, `.devin/scripts/`, `.devin/hooks.v1.json`,
  `AGENTS.md`, and skill files are read-only unless the user asks for
  that specific change.
- The user runs servers, migrations-adjacent processes, and installs —
  the agent runs migrations itself; never ask the user to run them.

## Evidence + claim contract (12-verification)

- DONE = observed world matches claimed world: symptom absent,
  expected state present with its external reference, blast-radius
  checked, claim scope ⊆ verified scope.
- CANDIDATE = code shipped + mechanistic verification only; never
  reported as fixed. Fix-verbs may not describe it.
- User-reported defect rejected → next action is reproduction, not
  another theory. `CANNOT-REPRO: <what you asked for>` is legal.
- `git diff` your own edits before blaming the environment.

## Security + performance invariants (05)

- Two authz planes: `staff authz plane` staff / `app authz (tenant plane)` group —
  never mix; unknown catalog key denies; fail closed; `group_id` on
  every resource load (IDOR); CSRF + Origin on cookie mutations; WS
  auth from the session cookie, never query-string tokens.
- No blocking I/O on the request path; tenant-scoped queries always filter
  the tenant key; cursor pagination; no N+1; no unbounded lists;
  fast serialization on request paths; multi-worker state through the
  shared-state helper, not module locals.
- Model change ⇒ a migration in the same slice, run by the agent.

## Analysis + report contract (15/16/11/14)

- Analysis asks are projects: declare the universe, walk all of it,
  hypothesis log (`found:`/`cleared:`/`unverifiable:`), constraint
  check before reporting. Items 25–29: quantifier asks get ask-side
  mechanical enumeration; units are elements × aspects; named
  analysis kinds get named passes; breadth asks carry volume floors;
  embedded plans get one row per finding.
- Implementations loop: analysis plan → traversal → findings →
  applied → re-verify, with the iteration record at `.unlazy/`.
- Reports are plain English with precise cites — a verdict the reader
  can't verify is a claim, not evidence.

## Trigger-load map — which file owns which domain

These files are trigger-loaded, not always-on. When the trigger
matches, read the file — it binds in full.

| trigger | file |
|---|---|
| Any UI/UX work — design, build, review, fix | `13-design-spec.mdc` then `09-design-review.mdc` + `ui-modularity.mdc` |
| Touching permissions, adapters, privileged-view | `security-authz.mdc` |
| Backend work under `app/` | `modularity-backend.mdc`, `performance.mdc` |
| Launching subagents / acting on their reports | `02-subagent-ceiling.mdc`, `06-subagent-gatecheck.mdc` |
| The user asks for an audit | `03-periodic-audits.mdc` |
| Living docs / product-port work | `04-rewrite-docs.mdc`, `07-product-transfer.mdc` |
| Running or debugging the server | `running-the-server.mdc` |
| Readability/refactor judgment | `08-code-quality.mdc` |

## The machinery that enforces this

`.devin/hooks.v1.json` + `.devin/scripts/stop-gate.mjs` arm ~75 checks
(session tracker, stop gate, item closure, cycle plan, deferral scan).
Their map lives in `10-rule-enforcement.mdc` (trigger-loaded — read it
when a check fires and you need the exact contract). The gate verifies
shape; the user grades depth.
